1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:01,338
A tick on your skin?

2
00:00:01,338 --> 00:00:03,023
Here's how to remove it safely.

3
00:00:06,250 --> 00:00:06,764
Step one.

4
00:00:06,764 --> 00:00:11,050
Use fine-tipped tweezers and grip the tick as close to the skin as you can.

5
00:00:13,250 --> 00:00:13,776
Step two.

6
00:00:13,776 --> 00:00:15,997
Pull straight up, slowly and steadily.

7
00:00:15,997 --> 00:00:17,517
Don't twist or squeeze it.

8
00:00:20,250 --> 00:00:20,855
Step three.

9
00:00:20,855 --> 00:00:24,709
Clean the bite and your hands with soap and water, or rubbing alcohol.

10
00:00:26,250 --> 00:00:26,855
Step four.

11
00:00:26,855 --> 00:00:30,789
Don't burn it, or smother it with petroleum jelly or nail polish.

12
00:00:30,789 --> 00:00:31,818
Just pull it out.

13
00:00:33,250 --> 00:00:37,342
Over the next few weeks, watch for a spreading rash, fever, or aches.

14
00:00:37,342 --> 00:00:40,604
If you get any, see a doctor and mention the tick bite.

15
00:00:40,604 --> 00:00:44,578
If part of the tick stays in, or you're unsure, get medical advice.
